{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Let them gather grain.</b> The overseers. And some say that the meaning of 'grain' is that it is with its stalks, but what seems correct to me is that it is called grain after the labor of winnowing or gathering. And he who says that the air of Egypt is humid because of the river, and [grain] would not keep there for seven years, could mix it with things that would preserve it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:42.872979685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}